{bpm: 172} {time: 4/4} {key: Am}

// Roman Numeral Notation Reference
// Key-independent chord charts - transpose by changing {key:}!
//
// Uppercase = Major, lowercase = minor
// I=1, ii=2, iii=3, IV=4, V=5, vi=6, vii°=7
//
// Edgar Allan Poe's "The Raven"

// ===== BASIC ROMAN NUMERALS =====
{label: intro}
i           iv          V           i           // i=Am, iv=Dm, V=E, i=Am
Once upon a midnight dreary, while I pondered, weak and weary,

// ===== UPPERCASE (Major) vs LOWERCASE (minor) =====
I           IV          V           I           // All major: I IV V I
Over many a quaint and curious volume of forgotten lore,
i           iv          v           i           // All minor: i iv v i
While I nodded, nearly napping, suddenly there came a tapping.

// ===== SEVENTH CHORDS =====
{label: verse1}
i           VI          III         V7          // V7 = dominant 7th
As of some one gently rapping, rapping at my chamber door.
i7          iv7         VII7        III7        // 7th chords on each degree
"'Tis some visitor," I muttered, "tapping at my chamber door."

// ===== FLAT ACCIDENTALS =====
i           ♭VI         ♭VII        i           // ♭VI, ♭VII (borrowed chords)
Ah, distinctly I remember it was in the bleak December;
i           bVI         bVII        i           // Same with 'b' instead of ♭
And each separate dying ember wrought its ghost upon the floor.

// ===== SHARP ACCIDENTALS =====
i           #iv         V           i           // #iv = raised 4th degree
Eagerly I wished the morrow; vainly I had sought to borrow
i           ♯iv         V           i           // Same with ♯ symbol
From my books surcease of sorrow—sorrow for the lost Lenore.

// ===== DIMINISHED =====
{label: bridge}
viio        vii°        viio7       vii°7       // Diminished (text & symbol)
Deep into that darkness peering, long I stood there wondering, fearing,
iio         ii°         #ivo        #iv°        // More diminished chords
Doubting, dreaming dreams no mortal ever dared to dream before.

// ===== SECONDARY DOMINANTS (Slash notation) =====
V/V         V/ii        V/vi        V           // V of V, V of ii, etc.
But the silence was unbroken, and the stillness gave no token,
V7/IV       V7/V        V7/vi       i           // Secondary dominant 7ths
And the only word there spoken was the whispered word, "Lenore?"

// ===== INVERSIONS (Slash chords) =====
{label: verse2}
i/III       iv/i        V/VII       i           // Chord over bass note
This I whispered, and an echo murmured back the word, "Lenore!"
I/V         IV/I        V/ii        I           // More inversions
Merely this and nothing more.

// ===== SUSPENDED & ADD =====
Isus4       Isus2       Vsus4       V           // Suspended chords
Open here I flung the shutter, when, with many a flirt and flutter,
Iadd9       IVadd9      Vadd9       I           // Add chords
In there stepped a stately Raven of the saintly days of yore.

// ===== AUGMENTED =====
I+          III+        V+          i           // Augmented triads
Not the least obeisance made he; not a minute stopped or stayed he;
Iaug        IIIaug      Vaug7       i           // Augmented variations
But, with mien of lord or lady, perched above my chamber door.

// ===== DURATION =====
{label: refrain}
i*2         V*2         i*4                     // Hold for beats
Quoth the Raven, "Nevermore."

// ===== KEY CHANGES =====
// Change {key:} to transpose everything!
{key: Em}
i           iv          V           i           // Now in E minor
And the Raven, never flitting, still is sitting, still is sitting

{key: Am}
i           iv          V           i           // Back to A minor
On the pallid bust of Pallas just above my chamber door;

// ===== NC (NO CHORD) =====
{label: outro}
i           NC*2        V           NC*2        // NC = silence
And my soul... (silence)... from out that shadow... (silence)

i*2         NC*1        V*1         i*4
Shall be... lifted... nevermore!

// ===== COMPLEX PROGRESSION =====
{bpm: 160}
i           ♭VI         ♭VII        V7/V
Take thy beak from out my heart,
V7          ♭VImaj7     ♭VII7       i
And take thy form from off my door!
iv          i/III       V7          i*4
Quoth the Raven... "Nevermore."

{loop: refrain 1}

